# =============================================================================
# Secrets
# =============================================================================
# Deny-by-default. Every .env is ignored and the template is added back by
# name, so a new .env.production or .env.staging is safe the moment it exists
# rather than the moment someone remembers to add a rule here.
.env*
!.env.example

# Service-account keys and certificates, matched by shape rather than by the
# specific names we happen to have used. gcloud will name a downloaded key
# whatever you ask it to.
*-key.json
*-sa.json
*-credentials.json
*-service-account*.json
serviceAccountKey.json
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore

# Emulator secret values. Committing this is how a real token leaks by accident.
.secret.local
# The same file for an extension, which is named after the instance rather than
# being a bare dotfile: `extensions/firestore-send-email.secret.local` holds the
# Resend API key for `firebase ext:dev` and does NOT match the rule above, since
# gitignore matches the whole name and not a suffix.
*.secret.local
# Legacy Cloud Functions runtime config; can contain tokens.
.runtimeconfig.json

# =============================================================================
# Build output and dependencies
# =============================================================================
node_modules/
dist/
out/
.next/
# The second dev server's output — see `dev:emulated:second` in
# apps/website/package.json. A separate directory is what lets it run alongside
# a server already using .next/.
.next-emulated/
# The spare server's output dir — see .claude/launch.json's -3200 entry. A peer
# session working in this same tree often already holds :3100.
.next-emulated-3200/
.next-emulated-3900/
.next-emulated-3250/
# The -3350 entry's output dir. On Sep 2 peer sessions held every other
# emulated port at once.
.next-emulated-3350/
# The -3450 entry's. Six emulated ports are now spoken for; a seventh will need
# a line here too, which is the cost of a `NEXT_DIST_DIR` per server.
.next-emulated-3450/
.next-real-3300/
.next-real-3400/
.next-real-3500/
.next-real-3600/
.next-real-3700/
.next-real-3800/
# Where a one-off `next build` is sent to check the static export without
# clobbering a peer session's .next/ or the committed-nothing `out/`. Not a
# server; delete it when the check is done.
.next-build-check/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The esbuild bundle for Cloud Functions. Anchored to that one directory on
# purpose: a bare `lib/` also matches apps/website/src/lib, which is source.
/functions/lib/

# =============================================================================
# Firebase
# =============================================================================
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
database-debug.log
ui-debug.log
pubsub-debug.log
dataconnect-debug.log

# =============================================================================
# Logs and editors
# =============================================================================
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# =============================================================================
# OS
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# Where `next dev --experimental-https` writes its self-signed cert. The *.pem
# rule above already catches the key itself; this covers the directory.
apps/website/certificates/

# =============================================================================
# The source documents for /about/future-plans
# =============================================================================
# Three files, 607 MB between them: the 1080p flythrough master, the June 2025
# renderings, and the 33-sheet December 2025 permit set. Every other original on
# this site is committed on purpose — see assets/README.md — and these are the
# exception, because half a gigabyte of architect's deliverable is not a thing
# to put in git history where it can never be taken out again.
#
# What ships instead is committed and small: ten WebP renderings under
# `apps/website/public/img/future/`, a 33 MB compressed cut of the flythrough
# under `apps/website/public/video/`, and the PNG stills they were built from in
# `assets/future/`. `assets/future/credits.json` records which document and
# which timestamp each one came from, so the derivation is checkable without the
# masters. Keep the masters — the parish paid for them — just not here.
assets/Future Plans/

# Scratch a Claude session writes into while working. Not output, not
# configuration — working notes, and there is no version of them worth keeping
# in the history. `.claude/launch.json` and the skills beside it ARE tracked, so
# this is scoped to the one directory rather than to `.claude/`.
.claude/scratch/
